            <ArticleTitle>Acrokerato - Elastoidosis Lineaius Manus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>298-299</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Variant of acrokerato elastoidosis characterized by linear, scaly, hyperkeratotic, fissured and transluscent papules on sides of thumbs and index fingers, was seen in 55 male patients, above the age, of fifty years. Actinic damage and repeated trauma were not evident. The term acrokerato - elastodosis linearis manus is suggested for this variant.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
